    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39461" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŭgillum</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρὰξ
			χειρός</span>, Gloss. Lat. Gr.), dim.
		pugnus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>what one can hold in the fist</i>, <i>a handful</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lentis pugillus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 158</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 22, 89, § 242</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 10, 152</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">melior est pugillus cum requie,</span>”
				<i>a very little</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Eccl. 4, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
